WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.352
This lecture completes school Seven C Part A sections four and five. We connect the physiology of exhaled carbon dioxide to ROSC recognition, resuscitation decisions and family communication.
本课完成学校7C Part A的第4和第5节，把呼出二氧化碳的生理联系到ROSC识别、复苏决策及家属沟通。

00:00:14.352 --> 00:00:26.496
The main textbook reading is integrated below in paired English and Chinese. It covers the named adult-arrest section and clearly labels older statements that differ from current local guidance.
下方已整合主教材的中英对照阅读，覆盖指定的成人骤停部分，并明确标示与现行当地指导不一致的较旧说法。

00:00:26.496 --> 00:00:39.384
No carbon-dioxide number independently proves a good outcome or authorizes stopping. Every interpretation needs the patient, signal quality, intervention history and applicable decision pathway.
任何二氧化碳数字都不能独立证明良好结局，或授权停止。每次解释都需要结合患者、信号质量、干预经过及适用决策路径。

00:00:39.384 --> 00:00:50.952
Our aim is a complete reasoning sequence: useful observation, justified action, reassessment and an accurate account to the team, clinical support and family.
本课目标是一条完整推理链：观察有用证据、采取有依据行动、复评，并向团队、临床支持及家属准确说明情况。

00:00:50.952 --> 00:01:02.208
Carbon dioxide is produced by metabolism and carried in blood to the lungs. It must reach ventilated lung units and then the sampling interface before the monitor can display it.
CO2由代谢产生，经血液运到肺，还必须到达有通气的肺单位和采样接口，监护仪才能显示。

00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:15.384
During CPR, compressions can generate some pulmonary blood flow. With ventilation and other factors reasonably stable, a change in flow may change the amount of carbon dioxide reaching the sensor.
CPR的按压可产生一定肺血流。在通气及其他条件相对稳定时，血流改变可能使到达传感器的CO2量随之改变。

00:01:15.384 --> 00:01:26.544
This is a physiological relationship, not a direct measurement of every organ's perfusion or metabolic viability. A low display can arise from several links in the chain.
这是一种生理联系，不是对每个器官灌注或代谢存活的直接测量。链上多个环节出问题，都可能使显示值降低。

00:01:26.544 --> 00:01:35.064
Ask where the chain could have changed before deciding what the number means. That prevents both false reassurance and premature pessimism.
判断数值意义之前，先问链上哪里发生了变化，才能同时避免虚假放心和过早悲观。

00:01:35.064 --> 00:01:50.040
A time capnogram plots exhaled carbon-dioxide concentration or pressure over time. The early expiration, rising phase, alveolar plateau and inspiratory fall help explain where the end-tidal value comes from.
时间型CO2图记录呼出CO2浓度或分压随时间变化。呼气早期、上升段、肺泡平台和吸气下降段，帮助解释ETCO2从哪里取得。

00:01:50.040 --> 00:02:02.664
Check that a plausible repeated waveform accompanies ventilation and that the displayed units and interface are understood. A disconnected line or poor sample can still create a misleading number.
应确认有与通气相符、合理重复的波形，并理解显示单位及接口。采样管脱接或样本不良时，仍可能看到误导数字。

00:02:02.664 --> 00:02:14.088
Waveform shape, frequency, baseline and change can add context. They do not substitute for observing chest movement, airway patency and the patient's circulation.
波形形态、频率、基线及变化可增加背景信息，但不能替代观察胸廓运动、气道通畅和患者循环。

00:02:14.088 --> 00:02:23.784
This school section focuses on arrest trends. Do not use a single altered waveform shape to diagnose one disease without the rest of the assessment.
本节重点是骤停趋势，不能仅凭一种异常波形形态，就在缺少其余评估时认定某个疾病。

00:02:23.784 --> 00:02:36.048
Continuous waveform capnography with clinical assessment is important for confirming and monitoring a tracheal tube. It also helps identify subsequent displacement or interruption of ventilation.
持续波形CO2结合临床评估，是核实及监测气管导管的重要手段，也有助识别后续移位或通气中断。

00:02:36.048 --> 00:02:49.992
A supraglottic airway or bag-mask interface may also provide sampled carbon dioxide, but leaks and sampling behavior differ. A number from one interface is not automatically equivalent evidence from another.
声门上气道或球囊面罩也可能采到CO2，但漏气及采样行为不同。一个接口取得的数值，不能自动视为与另一个接口具有相同证据意义。

00:02:49.992 --> 00:03:05.352
When the trace changes, check the patient and visible airway system promptly: seal, connections, tube position, secretions and sampling obstruction. Keep necessary oxygenation and circulation support going.
波形变化时，应迅速检查患者及可见气道系统，包括密封、连接、管位、分泌物及采样阻塞，同时继续必要氧合和循环支持。

00:03:05.352 --> 00:03:15.504
Evidence about a poor-prognosis cutoff in intubated adults must not be transferred to a mask or SGA as though the same test had been validated there.
关于气管插管成人不良预后界值的证据，不能直接转移到面罩或声门上气道，假装相同检测已经在这些接口得到验证。

00:03:15.504 --> 00:03:30.096
When production and circulation are stable, increased alveolar ventilation tends to lower carbon dioxide and reduced ventilation tends to raise it. Arrest physiology adds substantial flow and sampling limitations.
在产生量和循环稳定时，肺泡通气增加通常使CO2下降，通气减少通常使其升高；但骤停又加入显著的血流及采样限制。

00:03:30.096 --> 00:03:44.832
Therefore, do not teach that all underventilation produces a low ETCO2. A low sample with poor chest rise may reflect very little exhaled gas reaching the sensor rather than a simple blood-gas relationship.
因此不能教成所有通气不足都会使ETCO2降低。胸廓起伏差且采样值低，可能是到达传感器的呼出气体很少，并非简单的血气关系。

00:03:44.832 --> 00:03:58.704
Excessive ventilation may reduce venous return as well as wash out carbon dioxide. Deliberately ventilating faster to improve a saturation or reduce a number can worsen the circulation you are trying to support.
过度通气既可冲走CO2，也可能减少静脉回流。为了提高血氧或压低数字而刻意加快通气，可能反而损害正在支持的循环。

00:03:58.704 --> 00:04:12.960
Use the appropriate airway, rate and volume strategy and reassess actual ventilation. An isolated capnography target cannot justify ignoring chest rise, air entry or hemodynamics.
应使用适当气道、频率和容量策略，并复评实际通气。孤立CO2目标不能成为忽略胸廓起伏、进气或血流动力学的理由。

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:28.368
With the airway and ventilation reasonably consistent, a falling value may prompt review of compressor fatigue, depth, recoil, position and interruptions. Watch the technique instead of diagnosing poor CPR from the number alone.
气道和通气相对稳定时，ETCO2下降可提醒检查疲劳、深度、回弹、位置及中断。应真正观察技术，而不是仅凭数字诊断CPR质量差。

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:40.248
Correct an observed problem, such as leaning or an exhausted compressor, with a coordinated change that minimizes interruption. Then reassess the waveform and the rest of the resuscitation.
若观察到持续倚压或按压者疲劳，应通过协调更换等方法纠正，并尽量减少中断，再复评波形及整体复苏。

00:04:40.248 --> 00:04:52.320
A rise after improved compressions supports a useful response but does not prove every organ is adequately perfused. Patient factors, cause and ventilation still influence the result.
改善按压后数值升高，支持出现有用反应，但不能证明所有器官灌注都足够；患者因素、病因及通气仍会影响结果。

00:04:52.320 --> 00:05:04.080
Do not give an extra drug, excessive breaths or untrained compressions merely to reach a desired display. Quality monitoring should improve actual care rather than replace it.
不能只为达到某个显示值就额外给药、过量通气或采用未受训练的按压。质量监测应改善真实照护，而不是取代照护。

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:16.416
During a transfer, the trace suddenly falls after being stable. Do not decide immediately that circulation has failed or that the monitor is wrong; both patient and equipment need prompt assessment.
转移过程中，原本稳定的波形突然下降。不能马上断定是循环衰竭，也不能马上断定只是仪器错了；患者和设备都要及时检查。

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:31.008
Check ventilation, airway position and seal, visible connections and the sampling path while another clinician maintains effective CPR. Look for a change in the patient or a newly developing cause.
应在另一人维持有效CPR时，检查通气、气道位置及密封、可见连接和采样通路，并寻找患者改变或新出现的病因。

00:05:31.008 --> 00:05:42.720
If a connection is corrected and the trace returns, reassess the patient rather than assuming the entire problem is solved. A sampling fault and physiological deterioration can occur together.
若纠正连接后波形恢复，仍要复评患者，不能认定全部问题已解决。采样故障和生理恶化可以同时发生。

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:54.216
Report the time, preceding action, observed problem, correction and response. That creates a useful clinical trend instead of a collection of unexplained numbers.
应报告时间、此前动作、观察到的问题、纠正措施及反应，形成有意义的临床趋势，而不是一串无法解释的数字。

00:05:54.216 --> 00:06:05.064
An abrupt sustained increase can occur when spontaneous circulation delivers more accumulated carbon dioxide to the lungs. It is an important cue to announce to the team.
自主循环恢复后，更多积聚CO2可被送到肺，造成突然且持续的升高。这是应及时向团队通报的重要线索。

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:16.872
No absolute value of thirty-five or forty proves ROSC. Ventilation, airway changes, drugs, compressions and the arrest cause can also affect the trend.
并不是达到35或40就证明ROSC。通气、气道改变、药物、按压及骤停病因，也可能改变趋势。

00:06:16.872 --> 00:06:29.304
Check the context, look for other signs and coordinate a brief appropriate reassessment of circulation. Do not create repeated long pulse checks every time one breath produces a higher value.
应检查背景、寻找其他迹象，并协调适当短暂的循环复评。不能因为一口气数值高一点，就反复长时间停下来摸脉。

00:06:29.304 --> 00:06:41.304
If spontaneous circulation is confirmed, change to post-arrest care. If it is not confirmed, continue or promptly resume effective arrest care and investigate the change.
若确认自主循环，就转入骤停后照护；若没有确认，应继续或及时恢复有效骤停处理，并查明变化原因。

00:06:41.304 --> 00:06:53.904
The school highlights values below ten millimeters of mercury. Treat a persistent low value as a reason to review the resuscitation, not as direct proof of severe metabolic failure.
学校特别提醒低于10毫米汞柱的数值。持续低值应促使检查复苏过程，不能直接当成严重代谢衰竭的证明。

00:06:53.904 --> 00:07:08.400
Review compression quality and ventilation together, verify the waveform and interface, and reconsider reversible causes. Low pulmonary flow from an obstruction may not improve simply by telling the compressor to push harder.
应一起检查按压和通气，核实波形及接口，并重新考虑可逆病因。阻塞造成的低肺血流，不一定靠让按压者更用力就能改善。

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:22.104
Document what was assessed and corrected, and communicate an unresolved low trend early. A sentence saying CPR was excellent is less useful than actual observations and the response to correction.
要记录实际检查和纠正了什么，并及早通报未解决的低值趋势。笼统说“CPR很好”，不如记录真实质量观察及纠正后的反应有用。

00:07:22.104 --> 00:07:32.592
Do not stop on that number. Even a concerning prognostic association does not replace the local eligibility, consultation and discontinuation pathway.
不能因为这个数字就停止。即使它与不良预后有关，也不能替代当地的适用条件、咨询及终止复苏路径。

00:07:32.592 --> 00:07:43.968
A group of patients with a particular measurement can have worse outcomes without the measurement perfectly identifying every person who cannot survive. Prediction and certainty are different.
某测值人群总体结局较差，并不表示该测量能完美识别每个不可能生存的人。预测和确定性是不同概念。

00:07:43.968 --> 00:07:58.152
Current AHA guidance discusses a low value after prolonged intubated adult ALS only as one part of a multimodal decision. It specifically warns against a universal cutoff in nonintubated patients.
现行AHA只把较长时间插管成人ALS后的低值，作为多模态决定的一部分，并明确反对给未插管患者套用统一界值。

00:07:58.152 --> 00:08:10.824
A higher value is also not a guarantee that ongoing efforts will produce a favorable neurological result. Integrate the entire clinical course rather than using either side of a threshold as a verdict.
较高数值同样不能保证继续复苏会带来良好神经结局。应结合完整临床经过，而不是把界值的任何一边当成判决。

00:08:10.824 --> 00:08:21.696
For this course, the actual BCEHS pathway and appropriate clinical direction govern the stopping decision. We do not replace them with a textbook rhyme or foreign rule.
本课程的停止决定应依真实BCEHS路径及适当临床指导，不用教材口诀或其他地区规则替换。

00:08:21.696 --> 00:08:34.464
In our original case, the ETCO2 rises persistently and the patient begins normal breathing. The team announces the change and coordinates a brief appropriate assessment that confirms circulation.
在本原创病例中，ETCO2持续升高，患者开始正常呼吸。团队通报变化并协调适当短暂检查，确认自主循环。

00:08:34.464 --> 00:08:45.672
Do not confuse an organized rhythm alone, an occasional gasp or a pulse generated by the compressor with this confirmation. Those findings need their own clinical interpretation.
不能把仅有有序心律、偶发喘息或按压生成的脉搏，与这种确认混淆。这些所见都需要另外结合临床解释。

00:08:45.672 --> 00:08:59.040
If the assessment does not confirm circulation, promptly return to the indicated arrest response. A plan for ROSC must not create a prolonged no-flow interval in a patient who remains pulseless.
若检查没有确认循环，应及时回到有指征的骤停处理。准备ROSC方案，不能使仍无脉患者经历长时间无血流。

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:13.008
With confirmed ROSC, stop unnecessary compressions and immediately reassess airway, breathing, perfusion and neurological state. Continue monitoring because re-arrest remains possible.
确认ROSC后停止不必要按压，立即复评气道、呼吸、灌注及神经状态，并继续监测，因为仍可能再次骤停。

00:09:13.008 --> 00:09:25.944
Global ischemia and reperfusion can injure brain, myocardium and other organs. Restored circulation does not immediately repair the original cause or the consequences of low flow.
全身缺血及再灌注可损伤脑、心肌和其他器官。循环恢复，并不会立刻修复原发病因或低血流造成的后果。

00:09:25.944 --> 00:09:39.720
Maintain an effective airway and assess whether spontaneous breathing is adequate. An airway device that was tolerated during arrest may become inappropriate as consciousness and protective reflexes return.
应维持有效气道，并判断自主呼吸是否足够。骤停时耐受的气道器械，可能随着意识和保护反射恢复而不再适合。

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:54.048
Monitor rhythm and perfusion, check and address glucose as indicated, and reassess after every change. Prepare equipment and team roles for possible re-arrest rather than dismantling the response immediately.
应监测心律和灌注，按指征检查处理血糖，并在每次改变后复评。要保留应对再骤停的器械及角色安排，不能马上撤掉整个复苏准备。

00:09:54.048 --> 00:10:07.032
Communicate the arrest course and current instability to the receiving system. Suspected cause, ECG findings, clinical support and local destination rules together determine the appropriate transport plan.
应向接收系统通报骤停经过及当前不稳定。疑似病因、心电表现、临床支持和当地目的地规则，共同决定合适转运计划。

00:10:07.032 --> 00:10:20.904
During arrest and before reliable post-ROSC oxygen measurement, avoiding hypoxemia is essential. Do not abruptly reduce oxygen because a theoretical hyperoxia risk has become the only focus.
骤停期间，以及ROSC后尚无可靠氧测量时，避免低氧至关重要。不能只盯理论高氧风险，就突然盲目减少供氧。

00:10:20.904 --> 00:10:34.296
Once the measurement is reliable, use the applicable local target and titrate unnecessary excess. Saturation near its upper plateau does not reveal how high arterial oxygen has risen.
测量可靠后，应依适用当地目标滴定并减少不必要过量氧。饱和度接近上方平台，并不能显示动脉氧已经高到什么程度。

00:10:34.296 --> 00:10:49.536
Know the labelled source difference: N03 essentials use ninety-two to ninety-eight percent, whereas AHA twenty-twenty-five discusses ninety to ninety-eight after reliable measurement. Do not invent an averaged target.
要记清来源差异：N03要点为92%至98%，AHA 2025在可靠测量后讨论90%至98%。不能自行取平均目标。

00:10:49.536 --> 00:11:03.792
Consider signal quality, perfusion and the patient instead of treating one pulse-oximeter value as infallible. Continue oxygenation assessment and communicate uncertainty when the reading is unreliable.
应考虑信号质量、灌注及患者，而不能把一次血氧读数当成绝对正确。读数不可靠时，应继续评估氧合并通报不确定性。

00:11:03.792 --> 00:11:19.200
After ROSC, carbon dioxide influences cerebral blood flow. Excessively low arterial CO2 can constrict cerebral vessels, so purposeful hyperventilation is not a neutral way to improve a monitor number.
ROSC后CO2影响脑血流。过低的动脉CO2可使脑血管收缩，因此刻意过度通气，并不是无害地改善监护数字。

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:31.824
End-tidal and arterial values can diverge when perfusion, ventilation-perfusion matching and dead space change. A normal end-tidal number does not prove a normal arterial value.
灌注、通气血流匹配及死腔改变时，呼气末与动脉数值可能分离。ETCO2正常，并不能证明PaCO2正常。

00:11:31.824 --> 00:11:46.800
Current N03 has an internal target difference between its essentials and ACP paragraph. AHA's arterial range is a separately labelled recommendation, not a way to silently resolve the local end-tidal wording.
现行N03要点与ACP段的目标本身存在差异。AHA的动脉范围是另一项应标明来源的建议，不能用来默默消除当地呼气末文字差异。

00:11:46.800 --> 00:12:01.920
Use the current applicable clinical direction, monitor ventilation and avoid large reflex changes based on one value. Preserve these source distinctions in your study notes rather than memorizing a fabricated universal range.
应依当前适用临床指导监测通气，避免凭一次读数大幅反射性调整。学习笔记要保留这些来源区别，不能背一条编造的统一范围。

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:16.056
Avoid hypotension after ROSC and reassess actual perfusion. The oxygen-delivery chain still requires adequate forward flow; a good-looking saturation does not protect a poorly perfused brain.
ROSC后应避免低血压，并复评真实灌注。氧输送仍需要足够前向血流，血氧看着好也不能保护灌注不足的脑。

00:12:16.056 --> 00:12:32.112
The local N03 text contains differing systolic wording and a mean-pressure reference near sixty-five. AHA twenty-twenty-five uses at least sixty-five mean arterial pressure as a minimum, with individualized clinical context.
当地N03的收缩压文字有差异，并提供约65的平均压参考。AHA 2025采用平均动脉压至少65作为最低目标，同时仍要考虑个体背景。

00:12:32.112 --> 00:12:44.592
The textbook's generic one-to-two-liter bolus is not a universal order. Assess volume loss, pump function and response, and stay within the current local fluid plan and permissions.
教材笼统的一至两升液体，不是统一指令。要评估容量丢失、泵功能及反应，并遵守现行当地液体方案和权限。

00:12:44.592 --> 00:12:54.912
Persistent shock may require advanced clinician support. Understanding vasopressors in the reading does not give a PCP unrestricted permission to start an infusion.
持续休克可能需要高级临床支援。阅读中理解升压药，不代表PCP可以不受限制地自行开始输注。

00:12:54.912 --> 00:13:08.688
Do not deliberately cool every survivor with large cold-fluid boluses. Temperature management is a monitored strategy; traumatic injury and spontaneous hypothermia add important qualifications.
不能用大量冷液刻意给每位幸存者降温。温度管理是有监测的策略，创伤及自发低温又有重要特殊条件。

00:13:08.688 --> 00:13:21.552
A head-up position after ROSC may be useful when compatible with airway, perfusion and injury. This is not permission to elevate the head during ongoing arrest as a routine CPR technique.
ROSC后在气道、灌注及损伤允许时，头高位可能有益，但这不是常规在仍骤停时进行头高位CPR的许可。

00:13:21.552 --> 00:13:36.384
N03 says about ten minutes before post-ROSC twelve-lead acquisition, while its checklist says five to ten. AHA recommends as soon as feasible and highlights early false-positive patterns and repeat recordings.
N03写ROSC后约10分钟再采12导，链接清单写5至10分钟。AHA则建议可行时尽快，并提醒极早期假阳性及重复记录的价值。

00:13:36.384 --> 00:13:49.032
Do not combine those statements into an invented compromise clock. Use current local direction and communicate the actual time, tracing and clinical state without delaying urgent coordination.
不能把这些说法拼成自行折中的计时。应依现行当地指导，如实通报时间、图形及临床状态，不能延迟紧急协调。

00:13:49.032 --> 00:14:02.016
Withholding CPR concerns whether resuscitation should begin, including obvious death, applicable lawful direction and safety. Discontinuation concerns stopping efforts that are already underway.
不开始CPR，是关于是否应启动复苏，包括明显死亡、适用合法指示及安全因素；终止复苏则是停止已经开始的努力。

00:14:02.016 --> 00:14:14.880
Recognition of life extinct is the required assessment following the appropriate discontinuation process, except for the separate obvious-death situation. It is not simply another name for the decision to stop.
确认生命迹象消失，是适当终止复苏过程后所需的评估，另有明显死亡情形；它并不只是“决定停止”的另一个名字。

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:28.536
The school introduces these decisions together, but the current local R01, R02 and R03 assign distinct requirements. Keep the sequence and the evidence for each decision clear.
学校把这些决定联系起来介绍，但现行当地R01、R02及R03各有不同要求，必须明确每项顺序及证据。

00:14:28.536 --> 00:14:42.552
An isolated poor ETCO2, a family request or an elapsed timer cannot substitute for that whole pathway. Uncertainty is a reason to seek appropriate clinical support, not to invent criteria.
一次不佳ETCO2、家属要求或计时结束，不能替代完整路径。不确定时应寻求适当临床支持，不能自行创造标准。

00:14:42.552 --> 00:14:56.712
Current obvious-death examples include decomposition, dependent lividity or whole-body rigor, and specified injuries incompatible with life. A cold or stiff body is not automatically the same finding.
现行明显死亡例子包括腐败、尸斑、全身尸僵，以及特定与生命不相容的损伤。身体冷或僵硬，并不自动等同这些所见。

00:14:56.712 --> 00:15:12.792
An applicable lawful direction may include an advance directive, MOST, No CPR form or recognized No CPR identification. Verify relevance and authority rather than treating every paper or relative's statement as equivalent.
适用合法指示可能包括预先指示、MOST、不复苏表或认可的不复苏标识。要核实关联性和权限，不能把每张纸或亲属说法都当成同等效力。

00:15:12.792 --> 00:15:23.976
No CPR does not mean no appropriate care or no family support. Follow the applicable direction and care plan without turning the absence of CPR into abandonment.
不进行CPR，不表示不提供适当照护或家属支持。应依适用指示及方案，不能把不按压变成不管患者。

00:15:23.976 --> 00:15:37.824
If the criteria are unclear, start the appropriate care and seek CliniCall support under the guidance. Scene safety remains essential; clinical uncertainty does not require entering an unsafe scene.
标准不清时，应依指导开始适当处理并寻求CliniCall支持。现场安全仍然必不可少，临床不确定也不要求进入危险现场。

00:15:37.824 --> 00:15:58.128
For a PCP- or EMR-led arrest without ACP or CCP present, current R02 requires early CliniCall contact after initial CPR, analysis and indicated shocks. Initial care takes priority; the first call is not deferred until resuscitation seems hopeless.
在没有ACP或CCP到场的PCP、EMR主导骤停中，现行R02要求在初始CPR、分析及有指征电击之后及早联系CliniCall。初始处理优先，但不能等到觉得没有希望才第一次打电话。

00:15:58.128 --> 00:16:11.568
A designated team member can communicate while others maintain care. The consultation may clarify treatable causes and the plan for continued efforts, selected conveyance or later discontinuation.
可由指定成员通话，其他人继续照护。咨询可以明确可处理病因，以及继续复苏、选择性转运或后续终止的方案。

00:16:11.568 --> 00:16:21.624
A prior consultation may include standing direction for a specified later point. That is different from independently deciding to stop when a minimum duration passes.
先前咨询可能包含针对后续特定时点的持续有效指示，这与最低时长一到就自行决定停止不同。

00:16:21.624 --> 00:16:32.592
Communicate new findings or uncertainty that may change that direction. Do not treat a phone call as blanket legal immunity or permission to ignore a changed patient.
若有可能改变指示的新发现或不确定性，应及时通报。一次电话不是全面法律免责，也不允许忽略病情变化。

00:16:32.592 --> 00:16:45.024
Prepare the collapse and witness history, bystander actions, actual resuscitation times and initial rhythm. Distinguish facts from estimates and state when the history is uncertain.
应准备倒地及目击经过、旁观者行动、真实复苏时点及初始心律，区分事实与估计，并说明病史何处不确定。

00:16:45.024 --> 00:16:59.376
Summarize current physiology and care: compression quality, analyses and shocks, airway and ventilation, capnography trend, access or medicines actually given, and any period of ROSC.
应概述当前生理和处理：按压质量、分析及电击、气道通气、CO2趋势、真实给予的通路药物，以及曾有的任何ROSC。

00:16:59.376 --> 00:17:10.896
Report relevant causes and interventions with results, not merely that the Hs and Ts were done. A negative or unavailable assessment is different from a cause being excluded.
病因及干预应连同结果报告，不能只说“H和T做过了”。检查阴性或无法完成，与病因已经排除，是不同情况。

00:17:10.896 --> 00:17:22.416
Ask a clear question about the next plan and read back the direction, including conditions and timing. Document who gave it, what it authorized and what prompted later updates.
应明确询问下一步，并复述指示，包括条件和时间。记录谁给出指示、允许做什么，以及后续因何更新。

00:17:22.416 --> 00:17:37.128
R02 describes several rapid-discontinuation considerations, not a rule that a first nonshockable rhythm or low ETCO2 is enough. The prolonged-no-flow route requires all of its stated elements.
R02列出几类快速终止的考虑，不是最初不可电击或ETCO2低就足够。长时间无血流路径，必须符合其列出的全部要素。

00:17:37.128 --> 00:17:51.072
That route includes at least twenty minutes observed unresponsive and presumed pulseless before emergency-service arrival, no CPR during that period, absent signs of life and the specified nonshockable rhythm evidence.
该路径包括急救服务到达前至少20分钟被观察为无反应、推定无脉，其间没有CPR、没有生命迹象，并符合指定不可电击心律证据。

00:17:51.072 --> 00:18:08.184
The medical terminal-illness consideration describes imminent unavoidable death and unsuccessful expected CPR, not simply anyone with cancer or a chronic condition. Lawful direction and verified representative authority are separate considerations.
终末疾病考虑指临近且不可避免的死亡、预期CPR不会成功，不是所有癌症或慢性病患者。合法指示及经核实代表权限，又是另外的考虑。

00:18:08.184 --> 00:18:21.024
Do not apply these as independent student decisions. Consult through the actual pathway, preserve legal-direction distinctions and obtain clarification whenever authority or facts are uncertain.
不能把这些当成学生可独立决定的标准。应通过真实路径咨询，保留合法指示的区别，权限或事实不清时及时澄清。

00:18:21.024 --> 00:18:32.832
The general twenty-minute minimum pathway is different from the rapid prolonged-no-flow route. One describes a resuscitation interval; the other includes the pre-arrival no-CPR history.
一般20分钟最低时长路径，不同于快速路径中的长期无血流。一条描述复苏时段，另一条涉及到达前没有CPR的病史。

00:18:32.832 --> 00:18:45.480
Current R02 body requires all three: not witnessed by paramedics, EMRs or first responders, nonshockable throughout, and no ROSC at any time for any duration.
现行R02正文要求三项全部满足：不是由急救医护、EMR或FR目击，全程不可电击，并且任何时点、任何持续时间都不曾有ROSC。

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:55.968
Its diagram abbreviates the rhythm wording as initially nonshockable. Do not drop the stricter throughout requirement from the body when studying or presenting the case.
图中把心律简写为“初始不可电击”。学习或汇报时，不能因此丢掉正文更严格的“全程”要求。

00:18:55.968 --> 00:19:08.592
A bystander-witnessed event is not the same as an emergency-provider-witnessed event for that particular criterion. Document exactly who saw what, and do not stop simply because the clock reaches twenty.
对该项条件，旁观者目击不等于急救服务人员目击。要明确记录谁看见什么，不能只是计时达到20分钟就停止。

00:19:08.592 --> 00:19:22.728
R02 describes a thirty-minute minimum pathway for initially nonshockable arrests and forty minutes for initially shockable arrests. These are minimum considerations, not independent countdown-to-death rules.
R02对初始不可电击骤停描述30分钟最低时长路径，对初始可电击描述40分钟。这些是最低时长考虑，不是独立的死亡倒计时。

00:19:22.728 --> 00:19:35.904
A patient initially in VF does not become a twenty-minute-pathway patient merely because the latest analysis shows asystole. Initial rhythm and the entire resuscitation course remain relevant.
最初为室颤的患者，不会只因最近一次分析变心室停搏，就变成20分钟路径患者。初始心律和完整复苏经过仍然重要。

00:19:35.904 --> 00:19:49.080
Any transient ROSC must be reported; do not erase a brief circulation period because arrest recurred. Clarify how actual timing and changed circumstances affect the plan with clinical support.
任何短暂ROSC都必须报告，不能因为再次骤停就把那段循环抹掉。应向临床支持明确实际计时及变化如何影响方案。

00:19:49.080 --> 00:20:00.888
Continue the required treatment and assessment while using the appropriate consultation and standing direction. Do not invent clock resets or add drug rounds from an unrelated textbook rule.
使用适当咨询和持续指示期间，仍要继续所需处理及评估。不能自行编计时重置规则，也不能从不相关教材规则添加固定药物轮次。

00:20:00.888 --> 00:20:13.608
A duration only has meaning within the correct patient population and clinical pathway. Hypothermia, trauma and toxicological or other special circumstances may need a different approach.
时长只有放在正确患者人群和临床路径中才有意义。低温、创伤、中毒及其他特殊情况，可能需要不同处理。

00:20:13.608 --> 00:20:26.616
Confirm the actual care, rhythm course, signs of life, causes and response. A poorly delivered interval cannot be presented as a complete high-quality resuscitation simply because time elapsed.
要核实真实处理、心律经过、生命迹象、病因及反应。不能只因时间过去，就把质量不佳的一段描述为完成高质量复苏。

00:20:26.616 --> 00:20:45.936
R02 contains lawful- or verified-direction exceptions, while R03 asks for confirmation when CPR has been commenced. Preserve those source statements and promptly clarify the actual situation rather than inventing a universal exception or ignoring patient direction.
R02写有合法或经核实指示的例外，R03则要求已开始CPR者取得确认。应保留这些来源说法，及时澄清实际情境，不能自编统一例外，也不能忽略患者指示。

00:20:45.936 --> 00:20:59.328
Clinical consultation and accurate documentation support accountable care. Neither a rule nor a telephone call guarantees immunity, certainty of prognosis or permission to omit required assessment.
临床咨询及准确记录支持可问责照护，但无论规则还是电话，都不保证免责、预后绝对确定，或允许省略所需评估。

00:20:59.328 --> 00:21:15.072
Once the appropriate discontinuation process is complete, R03 specifies how life extinct is assessed. Except for obvious-death circumstances, at least two paramedics or EMRs are involved in independent confirmation.
适当终止复苏过程完成后，R03规定如何评估生命迹象消失。除明显死亡情形外，至少两位急救医护或EMR参与独立确认。

00:21:15.072 --> 00:21:27.336
This is not simply checking that the monitor is flat or pupils are fixed. The actual assessment specifies heart sounds, breathing observations and a central pulse over defined intervals.
这不只是看监护是否平线或瞳孔是否固定。实际评估规定了心音、呼吸观察和中心脉搏，并有明确观察时长。

00:21:27.336 --> 00:21:38.472
Keep noise and movement low enough for an adequate assessment, and record what each clinician actually found. Do not copy another provider's findings as your own examination.
应把噪声及运动降到足以准确评估的程度，并记录各人真实发现，不能把另一人的所见复制成自己的检查。

00:21:38.472 --> 00:21:49.176
Uncertainty means obtain further clinical direction. The generic pupil wording in the school summary is not a substitute for the currently served R03 procedure.
存在不确定时应进一步取得临床指导。学校总结中概括性的瞳孔说法，不能替代现行R03程序。

00:21:49.176 --> 00:22:02.928
The current R03 describes one clinician simultaneously listening for heart and breath sounds and observing respiratory effort for ninety seconds, while the second assesses the carotid pulse for ninety seconds.
现行R03描述：一人同期听心音、呼吸音并观察呼吸努力90秒，另一人同时检查颈动脉脉搏90秒。

00:22:02.928 --> 00:22:14.208
These are concurrent roles in a two-provider assessment, not the ordinary initial brief arrest-recognition check and not a reason to delay starting indicated CPR for ninety seconds.
这是双人评估中的同期分工，不是最初普通短暂的骤停识别检查，也不是应先等90秒再开始有指征CPR的理由。

00:22:14.208 --> 00:22:28.248
Its additional asystole or very slow PEA observation is labelled ACP and CCP, and ultrasound assistance is labelled CCP. Do not erase those scope labels when making a PCP study card.
附加的心室停搏或极慢无脉电活动监测，标明仅限ACP和CCP；超声辅助则标为CCP。制作PCP学习卡时不能删掉这些等级。

00:22:28.248 --> 00:22:39.768
Record the real assessment and times after the appropriate direction. Environmental hypothermia is an important exception and must not be forced through a routine ROLE checklist.
应在适当指导后记录真实评估及时间。环境性低温是重要例外，不能强行套普通ROLE表。

00:22:39.768 --> 00:22:52.632
In environmental hypothermia, absence of usual signs cannot be used routinely to record life extinct. Seek the appropriate clinical direction and rewarming-capable destination planning.
环境性低温中，通常生命征象缺失不能被常规用于记录生命迹象消失，应取得适当指导，并规划可提供复温的目的地。

00:22:52.632 --> 00:23:05.232
Traumatic arrest prioritizes particular reversible causes and has its own time-critical transport considerations. This adult medical-arrest lecture does not replace the traumatic pathway.
创伤性骤停优先处理特定可逆病因，并有自身时间紧迫的转运考虑；本成人内科骤停课不能取代创伤路径。

00:23:05.232 --> 00:23:17.592
A prediction rule from one population must not be used as certain evidence in another. Toxicological events and unusual circumstances require the relevant expertise and pathway.
一个人群中建立的预测规则，不能拿到另一人群当成确定证据。中毒及特殊情境需要相应专长和路径。

00:23:17.592 --> 00:23:32.448
If the scene history, legal direction, assessment or consultation plan is unclear, state the uncertainty and obtain clarification. Inventing a confident answer is not safer than communicating what is unknown.
若现场病史、合法指示、评估或咨询方案不清，应如实说明并澄清。编一个自信答案，不比沟通未知更安全。

00:23:32.448 --> 00:23:45.144
When staffing and circumstances permit, assign someone to explain what is happening and support the appropriate family or support person. Do not let all communication wait until a final decision.
人员和情境允许时，可安排一人解释当前情况，并支持适当家属或支持者，不能把所有沟通都拖到最终决定后。

00:23:45.144 --> 00:23:57.336
Ask about relationship, preferred name, language and cultural needs without assuming one family pattern. Arrange suitable interpretation rather than relying on medical jargon.
应询问关系、希望如何称呼、语言及文化需要，不能假定所有家庭都相同。应安排适当翻译，而不是依靠医学术语沟通。

00:23:57.336 --> 00:24:08.088
Acknowledge useful bystander actions, such as calling for help or attempting CPR, without guaranteeing that those actions will produce survival or blaming them for a poor outcome.
可以肯定呼救和尝试CPR等有用行动，但不能保证这些行动一定带来生存，也不能把不良结局归咎旁观者。

00:24:08.088 --> 00:24:20.448
Keep privacy and scene safety in view. Removing PPE is appropriate only when the clinical exposure risk permits it; a compassionate interaction must not require unsafe removal.
同时要保护隐私和现场安全。只有暴露风险允许时才适合脱去防护；有同理心的沟通不应要求不安全地摘除防护。

00:24:20.448 --> 00:24:33.768
After the appropriate process establishes death, give the news plainly and accurately. For example: I am very sorry. The treatment has not restored circulation, and Sam has died.
在适当程序确认死亡后，应清楚准确传达，例如：“非常遗憾，治疗没有使循环恢复，Sam已经死亡。”

00:24:33.768 --> 00:24:44.640
Avoid phrases that may imply sleep, temporary absence or that the person might still be alive elsewhere. Use a calm tone and the person's name when appropriate.
应避免让人误解为睡着、暂时离开，或仍在别处活着的说法。语气应平静，合适时使用逝者名字。

00:24:44.640 --> 00:24:56.952
Describe only the care actually provided. Do not say every possible intervention was tried, promise an exact cause of death, or claim advanced treatments that the team did not perform.
只能描述实际提供的照护。不能说试尽所有可能措施，不能保证确切死因，也不能声称做过团队未实施的高级治疗。

00:24:56.952 --> 00:25:08.280
Then pause. Remain present and listen rather than filling the silence with a long technical explanation. Offer practical next steps under the actual service process.
随后应停下来，留在现场倾听，而不是用长篇技术解释填满沉默。再依据真实服务程序提供实际后续安排。

00:25:08.280 --> 00:25:18.192
A family member asks whether anything else can be done. Acknowledge the shock and answer the actual question without becoming defensive or listing your credentials.
家属问还有没有其他办法时，应承认他们受到的冲击，并回答实际问题，不能转为防御或罗列资历。

00:25:18.192 --> 00:25:31.272
A truthful response may explain that the team provided the indicated treatment, obtained clinical direction and completed the required assessment, but circulation did not return. Match the statement to the facts.
如实回答可以说明团队提供了有指征处理、取得临床指导并完成所需评估，但循环没有恢复；具体措辞必须与事实一致。

00:25:31.272 --> 00:25:45.312
Do not imply the heart must have no electrical activity if the assessment involved PEA, or that a protocol can mathematically prove zero chance in every individual. Clear language need not create false claims.
若涉及无脉电活动，不能暗示心脏一定完全无电活动，也不能说流程能数学证明每个人机会都为零。清楚表达不需要制造不实说法。

00:25:45.312 --> 00:25:57.264
Allow further silence, answer honestly and explain what happens next within the actual process. Respectful presence is care; it is not an attempt to force acceptance immediately.
应允许继续沉默、诚实回答，并按真实程序解释接下来会发生什么。尊重地陪伴也是照护，不是强迫家属立即接受。

00:25:57.264 --> 00:26:10.968
Record actual times and clearly identify estimates. Include initial rhythm, changes, bystander and team interventions, pauses, shocks, airway findings and any transient ROSC.
应记录真实时点，并明确哪些是估计；包括初始心律、变化、旁观者及团队干预、暂停、电击、气道所见和任何短暂ROSC。

00:26:10.968 --> 00:26:23.592
Document observed CPR quality and the reasons for clinical choices. Do not state all reversible causes excluded when only a mnemonic discussion occurred or an assessment was unavailable.
应记录观察到的CPR质量及临床选择理由。若只是讨论口诀或无法检查，不能写所有可逆病因都已排除。

00:26:23.592 --> 00:26:37.488
Record clinical consultation and direction with its conditions, the applicable discontinuation basis and the actual ROLE findings, providers and times. A blank template is not evidence of an examination.
应记录临床咨询及其条件、适用终止依据，以及真实ROLE发现、人员和时间。空白模板本身不是完成检查的证据。

00:26:37.488 --> 00:26:50.256
Describe relevant family communication and the subsequent service steps honestly. Preserve the record and scene requirements; no procedure should be performed after death merely to gain practice.
应如实记录相关家属沟通及服务后续步骤，遵守记录和现场要求；不能在人已死亡后仅为练习而实施操作。

00:26:50.256 --> 00:27:05.304
In ending A, a sustained rise and the coordinated clinical assessment confirm ROSC. The team supports airway, ventilation and perfusion, communicates the course and plans definitive care while preparing for re-arrest.
A结局中，持续升高及协调临床评估确认ROSC。团队支持气道、通气和灌注，通报经过、规划最终照护，并继续防备再骤停。

00:27:05.304 --> 00:27:19.440
In ending B, the value stays low despite reviewed technique and no circulation is confirmed. The team continues appropriate care, investigates causes and uses the early consultation and applicable pathway.
B结局中，检查技术后CO2仍低，且没有确认循环。团队继续适当处理、寻找病因，并依据早期咨询及适用路径推进。

00:27:19.440 --> 00:27:33.864
Because this original patient initially had a shockable rhythm, an eventual asystolic analysis does not create eligibility for the general twenty-minute pathway. Communicate the whole course, not the last strip alone.
由于该原创患者最初可电击，即使后来一次分析为心室停搏，也不会因此符合一般20分钟路径。必须通报全过程，不能只报最后一条心电。

00:27:33.864 --> 00:27:47.016
Neither ending is decided by what the team hopes to see. The transition, continued care or eventual discontinuation must follow verified evidence, current direction and the correct sequence.
两种结局都不能按团队希望看到什么决定。转换、继续处理或最终终止，都必须依核实证据、当前指导和正确顺序。

00:27:47.016 --> 00:28:29.688
The assigned saturation page gives several contextual numbers: 97-100 percent as its usual reference, about 95 percent as an older-adult example, and a broader 92-100 percent practice statement. They are not interchangeable prescriptions for a post-arrest patient, nor proof that every person above 90 percent is safe. Compare the reliable reading with baseline, symptoms, oxygen support and the separately identified current N03 or other applicable pathway. The source also confuses hypercapnia with carbon-monoxide interference: carbon dioxide retention and carboxyhemoglobin are different problems.
指定血氧页列出多种有背景的数字：通常参考97至100%、老年人示例约95%，以及较宽的临床表述92至100%。它们不是可互换的骤停后处方，也不证明每个人超过90%就安全。应把可靠读数与基线、症状、氧疗支持及已另行标示的现行N03或其他适用路径比较。来源还把高碳酸血症与一氧化碳干扰混淆；二氧化碳潴留和碳氧血红蛋白是不同问题。

00:28:29.688 --> 00:29:08.184
Choose a sensor designed for the patient, site and monitor: an adult spring clip is not automatically suitable for a small infant, and a wrap, ear or forehead sensor has its own placement and compatibility instructions. Inspect skin, alignment, attachment and signal quality rather than taping any probe anywhere. An inflating blood-pressure cuff can interrupt the pulsatile signal on that limb; do not interpret the concurrent lost or falling oximeter signal as a new diagnosis before checking that interaction. A different site may help, but does not guarantee accuracy in low perfusion.
应选适合患者、部位及监护仪的探头：成人弹簧夹不自动适合小婴儿，包裹式、耳部或额部探头各有定位和相容说明。要检查皮肤、对准、固定与信号质量，不能任意把任何探头贴到任何部位。同一肢体的血压袖带充气会打断搏动信号；在核对这个相互影响前，不能把同时丢失或下降的血氧信号当新诊断。换部位可能有帮助，却不保证差灌注时准确。

00:29:08.184 --> 00:29:49.320
Explain all five assigned pressure factors as interacting variables: cardiac output supplies flow; arteriolar resistance opposes it; circulating volume influences venous return; viscosity affects resistance; and large-artery elasticity permits expansion and recoil. Compliance is change in volume for a change in pressure, not another name for peripheral resistance. A stiff artery, a constricted arteriole and thickened blood are different mechanisms. The source alternates elasticity and rigidity in a way that can reverse the meaning: less arterial compliance generally means more stiffness, not improved cushioning.
把指定的五个血压因素解释成相互作用变量：心排提供血流，小动脉阻力阻碍血流，循环血量影响静脉回流，黏度影响阻力，大动脉弹性允许扩张及回缩。顺应性是压力改变时容积的改变，并不是外周阻力的另一个名称。僵硬动脉、收缩的小动脉及黏稠血液是不同机制。来源交替使用弹性和僵硬度，可能把意义颠倒；动脉顺应性降低一般表示更僵硬，而不是缓冲更好。

00:29:49.320 --> 00:30:29.712
The volume paragraph describes atrial stretch and a faster-rate response. Distinguish that atrial or Bainbridge input from the arterial baroreflex, where increased arterial stretch usually promotes a slowing response. One paragraph does not mean more fluid always improves pressure or that every increased pressure produces tachycardia. For the weekly case, repeat a reliable pulse, pressure and clinical assessment after the actual intervention; explain whether flow, resistance, measurement conditions or several links may have changed. Do not select a fluid or vasodilator solely from one simplified factor.
血量段描述心房牵张及心率加快反应。要把这个心房即Bainbridge输入与动脉压力反射分开：后者动脉牵张增加通常促进减慢反应。不能据一段文字认更多液体总改善血压，或每次血压增加都会心动过速。本周病例中，真实干预后要重复可靠脉搏、血压及临床评估，解释改变的可能是血流、阻力、测量条件还是多个环节。不能只按一个简化因素选补液或扩血管药。

00:30:29.712 --> 00:31:19.272
The ending glossary adds legal vocabulary. Absconding is the source term for leaving an inpatient setting without permission, not an independent ambulance power to confine someone. False imprisonment concerns confinement without consent or lawful authority. The source distinguishes assault as threatened harmful contact and battery as intentional harmful or offensive contact. This U.S.-style distinction is not a complete Canadian offence map: Criminal Code section265 includes intentional force without consent and specified attempts or threats. An intentional tort is a civil-wrong category, not a synonym for every treatment error or criminal charge. Assess consent, safety and the real applicable authority instead of deciding from a label.
末页术语加入法律词汇。Absconding在来源中指未获许可离开住院环境，不是救护人员独立拘束权限。False imprisonment涉及无同意或合法权限的限制。来源区分assault为有害接触威胁、battery为故意有害或冒犯接触；这套美国式区别不是加拿大罪名完整图，加拿大《刑法》265条包含未经同意故意施力，以及特定尝试或威胁。Intentional tort是故意侵权的民事类别，不是每个治疗错误或刑事控罪同义词。应评同意、安全及真实权限，不能只套标签。

00:31:19.272 --> 00:32:08.664
Keep other glossary concerns distinct. Fraud concerns deception; the source uses libel for a damaging published falsehood. Neither one-line entry is a complete legal test. Malpractice concerns professional care failing the applicable duty or standard, not proof that a poor outcome alone establishes wrongdoing. Confidentiality protects entrusted information but is not a promise that relevant information can never be shared lawfully. Duty to warn raises a protection-and-disclosure question; it is not permission to broadcast a diagnosis or treat every angry statement as one universal legal trigger. Record facts, protect information and obtain appropriate guidance through the actual BC clinical/legal-service framework.
其余术语也应分开。Fraud涉及欺骗，来源以libel称损害声誉的已发表虚假内容；一句定义都不是完整法律判断。Malpractice涉及专业照护不符合适用义务或标准，不表示坏结局本身就证明失当。Confidentiality保护受托信息，不承诺相关信息永不能依法共享。Duty to warn提出保护及披露问题，不允许广播诊断，也不能认每句愤怒话都是同一法律触发。应记事实、护信息，并通过真实BC临床或法律机构框架取得适当指导。

00:32:08.664 --> 00:32:53.376
The first boundary page introduces forensic psychiatric nursing: appropriately qualified assessment, evidence handling, testimony and links to rehabilitation or social services can connect health care with justice systems. These are different tasks, not a qualification gained by reading the paragraph. A paramedic can accurately document observed behaviour, injuries, statements and care while preserving consent, dignity and the actual evidence pathway. Do not declare legal fitness, criminal responsibility or psychiatric diagnosis from a difficult interaction. U.S. insurance and benefits examples remain source context, not a reason to ration emergency assessment by presumed ability to pay.
首个边界页介绍法医精神护理：合格评估、证据处理、作证及康复社会服务衔接，可连接医疗与司法。这些是不同任务，不是读一段就获得的资质。救护人员可准确记观察行为、伤情、陈述及照护，同时维护同意、尊严和真实证据流程。不能从困难互动宣告法律适格、刑事责任或精神诊断。美国保险福利示例仍只是来源背景，不能按推测支付能力分配急救评估。

00:32:53.376 --> 00:33:03.624
Explain an abrupt rise, persistent low value and sudden drop with at least two possible mechanisms each. State what you would assess before changing the plan.
应能为突然升高、持续低值和突然下降，各解释至少两个可能机制，并说明改方案前要评估什么。

00:33:03.624 --> 00:33:13.200
Demonstrate the transition after confirmed ROSC and keep arterial versus end-tidal measurements and local versus AHA targets clearly labelled.
应能演示确认ROSC后的处理转换，并明确区分动脉与呼气末测量、当地目标与AHA目标。

00:33:13.200 --> 00:33:25.992
Then explain withholding, the rapid and general discontinuation pathways, early consultation and the current concurrent ninety-second ROLE assessment without substituting one number for the process.
再说明不开始、快速及一般终止路径、及早咨询，以及现行同期90秒ROLE评估，不能用一个数字替代整个过程。

00:33:25.992 --> 00:33:38.280
Finish by giving a concise consultation, a factual record and a clear compassionate family explanation. That completes the five saved Seven C teaching sections as a connected course.
最后应能完成简明咨询、事实记录，以及清楚且有同理心的家属说明。这样才把保存的7C五节正文连成完整教学。
